00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:35.067 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, on the other hand, I
have an 18 year old daughter

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:37.036
and a 21 year old son.

00:10:37.036 --> 00:10:41.574
Now, my only concern
honestly is for them.

00:10:41.574 --> 00:10:43.976
I don't even care about
like my extended family

00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:47.146
or my sisters, they know
who I am, they know me.

00:10:47.146 --> 00:10:51.917
And when people make false
allegations or attack you,

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:56.889
you know, my kids are so
used to it that honestly,

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.092
at this point I don't
even go to them with it

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:01.627
because they usually
don't hear about it.

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:04.797
My son will hear about it
only if it's on Barstools.

00:11:04.797 --> 00:11:06.966
"Dad, you're on
Barstools today."

00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:10.403
I'm like, okay, that means,
I guess I've made it, right?

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:12.171
- A sign of the times man.

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:15.408
- Thankfully, they don't care.

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:19.545
Sometimes I have to explain
to them and I remind them too

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:24.316
that there might
be people that know

00:11:24.316 --> 00:11:27.753
that they're related to
me, that they're my kids,

00:11:27.753 --> 00:11:31.457
that may not like me
and I always warn them

00:11:31.457 --> 00:11:33.459
the upside and downside.

00:11:33.459 --> 00:11:36.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a lot of upside
for them, but that for me,

00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:38.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't grow up
with famous parents.

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:40.933
I grew up with my mom,
a prison guard, my dad,

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:44.336
a family court probation guy
and a waiter on the weekends.

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:47.773
So it's very different, but
it's all they've known also.

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:52.344 align:start size:97% position:3%
They've been at events with
20 plus thousand people

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:54.380 align:start size:81% position:19%
at arenas that
I've been hosting.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:59.051 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they've seen the people
that are also invested as I am

00:11:59.051 --> 00:12:02.254 align:start size:88% position:13%
in what I love the most,
which is this country

00:12:02.254 --> 00:12:04.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the things that I
believe in and the passion

00:12:04.957 --> 00:12:07.026 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the freedom and
the liberty of America

00:12:07.026 --> 00:12:10.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the dream that is America,
because I am that dream.

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:13.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, I could
talk more about that later

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:15.334 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you want but, so I don't
have the switch, I don't care.

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:18.437
I care about my kids when
they're impacted by it.

00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:20.873
Everyone else, I don't care.

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:23.142
- So you mentioned a little
bit about your upbringing--

00:12:23.142 --> 00:12:26.779 align:start size:97% position:3%
- By the way, one sec,
don't ever hit Google alert

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:29.982 align:start size:97% position:3%
that says Dave Rubin, don't
put that on your phone.

00:12:29.982 --> 00:12:31.917
Don't read Twitter.

00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:35.187
I can't even, I have no access
to my social media accounts.

00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:37.289 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have to go through
an army of people

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:40.226
before I can send out my own
tweet, I have no passwords.

00:12:40.226 --> 00:12:43.028 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Now I see how you
have that great hairline

00:12:43.028 --> 00:12:44.563
because you're not on Twitter.

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:48.367
That's clearly the answer,
that's clearly the answer.

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:50.436
So a couple of weeks
ago I was on the show

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:53.472 align:start size:88% position:13%
with you with Dan
Bongino and I mentioned,

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:55.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
I was Googling something
right beforehand

00:12:55.474 --> 00:12:57.309
and I saw that you were
born in New York city.

00:12:57.309 --> 00:12:59.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
It turned out that
Dan was born in Queens

00:12:59.411 --> 00:13:02.081
and I was born in Brooklyn
and I mentioned it on air.

00:13:02.081 --> 00:13:03.883 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I thought, you know,
maybe there really is

00:13:03.883 --> 00:13:06.485
something there that
people born in New York

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:08.287
for as out of whack,

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:10.856
especially as New York
city under DeBlasio is,

00:13:10.856 --> 00:13:12.124
and Cuomo is governor,

00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:14.093 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
for as out of whack
as New York is,

00:13:14.093 --> 00:13:17.997 align:start position:0% line:0%
maybe there really is something
special about New York.

00:13:17.997 --> 00:13:19.899 line:0%
Can you talk about
that a little bit?

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:20.833 line:0%
Because you're a
true New York guy.

00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:22.301
You still live in New York.

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:24.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You can add to that
like Bill O'Reilly, right.

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:26.939
You can add to that
a guy Tom Leykis.

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tom Leykis was a highly
successful host nationally

00:13:30.009 --> 00:13:33.245
and started and spent a lot
of his career in Los Angeles.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:38.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
It probably has to do
with being very outspoken.

00:13:39.652 --> 00:13:43.022 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now I left New York and
pursued a whole other life.

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:46.692
I was out of New York 16
years and I started radio.

00:13:46.692 --> 00:13:49.195 align:start size:84% position:16%
You probably weren't
born yet Dave.

00:13:49.195 --> 00:13:53.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
1987 was the first time I
got behind a radio microphone

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:54.600
Close?

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.035
- I was 11 Hannity, come on.

00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:58.604 align:start size:72% position:28%
- You what?
- 11.

00:13:58.604 --> 00:14:01.473
- Oh you were 11, okay you
look great, you know why?

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.843
Cause you have a lot
slicker hair than I do

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:05.611
and you've gotta be
using Just for Men

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:08.280
and I've never used Just
for Men, so I'm teasing.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.282 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No nothing, this
is all natural.

00:14:10.282 --> 00:14:12.651
- All natural, you
got it right here.

00:14:12.651 --> 00:14:14.820 align:start size:97% position:3%
And some people used to
write me "Is your hair real?"

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.289 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'd be pulling it
on air, yeah, it's real.

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:22.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
But you know, I like
outspoken people.

00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:26.732 align:start size:97% position:3%
I like people that are not
afraid to express their views.

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:29.034
And honestly, if you
go through your life

00:14:29.034 --> 00:14:34.039
and you care about what
people think about you

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:38.210
and it stifles you
and it silences you

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.014
and it boxes you in, either--

00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:44.450
I always say on radio and TV,

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.852
I'm on the air four hours a day.

00:14:46.852 --> 00:14:50.489
This is all extemporaneous our
discussion here today, right?

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:55.494
And you can't fake it
for four hours a day.

00:14:55.494 --> 00:14:58.564
People see through
BS, they see it.

00:14:58.564 --> 00:15:02.601
And what you hear and what
you see is what you get.

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:05.304
Radio is more of a
warmth heart medium.

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:07.840
I have three hours,
TV I have an hour.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.542
It's fast paced,
it's a lot of news.

00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:13.012
We're getting a ton
of information in it

00:15:13.012 --> 00:15:15.581
and I feel like we're doing work

00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:17.616
that nobody else in
the media is doing.

00:15:17.616 --> 00:15:19.985
People like yourself and
you mentioned Dan Bongino

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:21.654
help out a lot.

00:15:21.654 --> 00:15:24.189 align:start position:0%
You know, you've been a
phenomenal addition to the show.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:27.026 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, but I don't want
to live my life,

00:15:27.026 --> 00:15:32.031
giving a flying rip what
some idiot keyboard warrior

00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:36.235
in their underwear in
their parents' basement

00:15:36.235 --> 00:15:40.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
at 60 years old cares
about me or says about me

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:43.275
anonymously on some
social media site.

00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:45.210
That's why I have no
access to any of it.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.679
I don't ever read it.

00:15:46.679 --> 00:15:48.948 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You just handed us the
clip, that's the promo clip.

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:52.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, that was a tailor
made promo clip right there.

00:15:52.251 --> 00:15:53.719
The guy in his underwear.

00:15:53.719 --> 00:15:57.289
- Not me, the keyboard
warriors that are psycho.

00:15:57.289 --> 00:15:58.757
- Oh not you you.

00:15:58.757 --> 00:16:01.293
- No not Hannity, Hannity
is not in his basement

00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:04.330
in his underwear anonymously
typing out I hate Hannity.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.864
That's not me.

00:16:05.864 --> 00:16:09.034
- Oh, alright, well they'll
still come after you for it.

00:16:09.034 --> 00:16:11.203 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Probably.
- Does the grind of it,

00:16:11.203 --> 00:16:13.505
the fact that you're doing
all those hours on the radio,

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:15.908
then you're doing
your hour at night

00:16:15.908 --> 00:16:18.644
and that you always have
to have something to say,

00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:20.879
and I know with you
that it is authentic,

00:16:20.879 --> 00:16:23.882
but that the, you know,
we went from, you know,

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:25.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
network news to
ultimately cable news.

00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:28.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then it was 24 hours
and now in effect

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:30.522 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's every time
Trump tweets, I mean,

00:16:30.522 --> 00:16:32.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're in a five
second news cycle now.

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:33.826
Do you think any of that

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
is actually part of
the problem right now?

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:39.798
Sort of why we're all kind
of crazed about politics?

00:16:39.798 --> 00:16:42.501 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm for more information,
not less information.

00:16:42.501 --> 00:16:45.337
I could tell you when I
first started in radio,

00:16:45.337 --> 00:16:47.106
I mentioned the light
went on first time.

00:16:47.106 --> 00:16:50.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
I believe it was 87,
no later than 88,

00:16:50.309 --> 00:16:54.246
which makes me 32 plus years
in radio, that's a long time.

00:16:54.246 --> 00:16:59.218
And I remember my first
professional radio gig

00:16:59.218 --> 00:17:01.887 align:start position:0%
where I actually got some money
was in Huntsville, Alabama.

00:17:01.887 --> 00:17:03.288
I started in California.

00:17:03.288 --> 00:17:04.723
And by the way, with
anyone starts on radio,

00:17:04.723 --> 00:17:05.958
you're terrible.

00:17:05.958 --> 00:17:07.626
And I was trying to, you know,

00:17:07.626 --> 00:17:10.129
I guess I wasn't as authentic.

00:17:10.129 --> 00:17:14.366 align:start position:0%
There's a great scene in
Howard Stern's "Private Parts."

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:17.770
That's my life, I lived
the same life he did.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.238
- I've seen it a billion times.

00:17:19.238 --> 00:17:20.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Except I do a different
form of radio, right?

00:17:20.806 --> 00:17:23.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's very different, but
I know what it's like

00:17:23.175 --> 00:17:24.643
when you start out on radio.

00:17:24.643 --> 00:17:26.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
"All right, here's the
weather, hazy, hot, humid,

00:17:26.879 --> 00:17:28.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
a chance of late
afternoon thunderstorms.

00:17:28.647 --> 00:17:33.018
Right now it's 78 degrees,
sunny, a chance of storms

00:17:33.018 --> 00:17:36.021
and more of the hits
of the 70s, 80s and 90s

00:17:36.021 --> 00:17:39.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming up right here on
WWWW," or whatever, right.

00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:40.559
You just want--

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:43.195
- Remember, it was WNBC.

00:17:43.195 --> 00:17:45.330
- It would be in his case, yeah.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:49.468
But he shows that and I did
that I mean, when I started.

00:17:49.468 --> 00:17:50.936
You're terrible when you start.

00:17:50.936 --> 00:17:54.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
It was interesting because
you're starting in this whole,

00:17:54.773 --> 00:17:59.578
there's a whole other path
that wasn't open to somebody

00:17:59.578 --> 00:18:02.881
like myself, but there
were more opportunities.

00:18:02.881 --> 00:18:05.951
There actually were
talk radio stations

00:18:05.951 --> 00:18:07.553
that hired young guys,

00:18:07.553 --> 00:18:11.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of like the farm
league that maybe one day

00:18:11.023 --> 00:18:13.225
some of them might be able
to get to a bigger market.

00:18:13.225 --> 00:18:15.394
And you know, I started
to get thrown out of town

00:18:15.394 --> 00:18:17.029
in California, I deserved it.

00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:19.665
Totally, you know, awful.

00:18:19.665 --> 00:18:24.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
I go to Huntsville, Alabama,
I arrived there in 1990.

00:18:26.138 --> 00:18:29.108
And then I worked there two
years and I went to audition

00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:32.478
in Atlanta for two
nights, I got hired.

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:35.180 align:start size:97% position:3%
I spent four wonderful years
in the city of Atlanta.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.448
I'd love to talk about that.

00:18:36.448 --> 00:18:41.253
I got to know these
civil rights leaders.

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:43.722 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, we recently
lost John Lewis.

00:18:43.722 --> 00:18:47.092
I have nothing politically
that I agree with John Lewis,

00:18:47.092 --> 00:18:50.662
except that in the
first day in Atlanta,

00:18:50.662 --> 00:18:52.865
I got a call to my radio show

00:18:52.865 --> 00:18:55.067
from then mayor Maynard Jackson.

00:18:55.067 --> 00:18:59.171 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I got to know
Joseph Lowery, the SCLC.

00:18:59.171 --> 00:19:00.405
They all come on my program.

00:19:00.405 --> 00:19:02.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
The mayor would
come on my program.

00:19:02.107 --> 00:19:04.576
Hosea Williams was my
favorite guest ever,

00:19:04.576 --> 00:19:07.579
a really close friend of
Martin Luther King Jr.

00:19:07.579 --> 00:19:09.848
John Lewis, Andy Young,

00:19:09.848 --> 00:19:11.850
and I don't think
Andy liked me much,

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:15.087
but with all these guys,
I knew when I got to know

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:18.490
their story and it was one of
great courage and conviction.

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:21.693
And if you look at
Selma to Montgomery,

00:19:21.693 --> 00:19:24.463 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you look at fire
hoses and dogs,

00:19:24.463 --> 00:19:25.864
and I learned this lesson,

00:19:25.864 --> 00:19:29.368
you see the peaceful
protest of that time.

00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:34.373
They helped make this
a more perfect union.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.109
They put it all on the line.

00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:39.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's an interesting side
note to this, you know,

00:19:39.444 --> 00:19:42.347 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we watched
the eulogy with Obama.

00:19:42.347 --> 00:19:47.352
The eulogy Obama gave it at
the John Lewis remembrance

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:51.657
and all the politics
that he brought up,

00:19:51.657 --> 00:19:53.625
which I found outrageous.

00:19:54.593 --> 00:19:56.261
- It was a political speech.

00:19:56.261 --> 00:19:58.463
- It was, it was awful.

00:19:58.463 --> 00:20:00.599
But he talked about the
John Lewis extension

00:20:00.599 --> 00:20:02.301
of the Voting Rights Act.

00:20:02.301 --> 00:20:05.137 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I'm thinking,
well, hang on a second,

00:20:05.137 --> 00:20:07.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
because the guy that's leading
your ticket, Joe Biden,

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:12.144 align:start size:84% position:16%
the ever corrupt,
ever forgetful, ever
out of it Joe Biden.

00:20:12.144 --> 00:20:16.949
Well, Joe Biden says his
mentor and his dear friend

00:20:16.949 --> 00:20:21.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
was Robert Bird,
the former Klansman.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
By the way, Hillary
said it, Bill said it,

00:20:23.989 --> 00:20:26.491
Schumer said it, Pelosi said it.

00:20:26.491 --> 00:20:31.129 align:start size:88% position:13%
So former president
Obama was talking about

00:20:31.129 --> 00:20:34.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
these historic bills that
John Lewis absolutely

00:20:34.032 --> 00:20:36.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
along with so many
others bravely fought for

00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:38.203 align:start size:81% position:19%
and made us a more
perfect union.

00:20:38.203 --> 00:20:40.439
Not perfect, we still
have a long way to go.

00:20:40.439 --> 00:20:43.642 align:start size:84% position:16%
And yet they're
talking about the act,

00:20:43.642 --> 00:20:47.646
but the guy that's running
actually supported the guy

00:20:47.646 --> 00:20:51.149
that filibustered that
historic legislation.

00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:53.785
People don't know and
this drives me nuts.

00:20:53.785 --> 00:20:55.988
Every two years,
every four years,

00:20:55.988 --> 00:20:57.522
what do they say
about Republicans?

00:20:57.522 --> 00:21:00.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's every election cycle,
Republicans are racist,

00:21:00.259 --> 00:21:03.428 align:start position:0%
sexist, misogynist, homophobic,
xenophobic, Islamophobic.

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:07.132 align:start size:97% position:3%
They want dirty air and
water, a Paul Ryan lookalike.

00:21:07.132 --> 00:21:09.635
There'll probably be a Donald
Trump look alike this year,

00:21:09.635 --> 00:21:11.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
is going to take
granny in a wheelchair

00:21:11.603 --> 00:21:15.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
after she's only eating
dog or cat food for a year

00:21:15.207 --> 00:21:17.776
and throw her over the
cliff in the wheelchair.

00:21:17.776 --> 00:21:21.647
That's every two and four
years, it is atrocious.

00:21:21.647 --> 00:21:24.082
I went through on
Hannity this week

00:21:24.082 --> 00:21:26.551 align:start size:97% position:3%
a history of how this happens
every two and four years.

